finition": "(poker, slang) A metaphorical place where a player goes to contemplate a decision; see in the tank.", "tags": ["slang"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(rail transport) Ellipsis of tank engine or tank locomotive.", "tags": ["abbreviation", "alt of", "ellipsis"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Before their conversion to 4-6-0 tender locomotives, the L.B. & S.C.R. Baltic tank engines Nos. 330 to 334 measured 50 ft. 5 in. over buffers; the nearest present approach to this figure is the 49 ft. 10½ in. of the remaining ex-Lancashire & Yorkshire Hughes type 4-cylinder 4-6-4 tanks of the L.M.S.R. The Furness and G. & S.W.R. 4-6-4 tanks of the same company, all now scrapped, were, respectively, 49 ft. 1½ in. and 47 ft. 8 in. long.", "reference": "1941 September, “The Why and the Wherefore: The Longest Tank Locomotives”, in Railway Magazine, pages 431–432:"}, {"text": "Representing the older types now are some Stroudley 0-6-0 tanks, while a Drummond \"C14\" 0-4-0 tank might still be pottering about on the Town Quays as of yore.", "reference": "1952 February, R. A. H. Weight, “A Railway Recorder in Wessex”, in Railway Magazine, page 133:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(clothing) Ellipsis of tank top.", "tags": ["abbreviation", "alt of", "ellipsis"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "T-BACK COTTON TANK", "reference": "1990 November 18, “Earl’s Reebok Sale for the Holidays”, in Granite City Press-Record Journal, volume 6, number 46, Granite City, Ill., →OCLC, page 8A:"}, {"text": "It pleased her more than she could say to know she walked on her own land, over dewed grass, wearing a tank and cotton pajama pants.", "reference": "2008, Nora Roberts, Tribute, New York, N.Y.: G. P. Putnam’s Sons, →ISBN, page 206:"}, {"text": "I was wearing a tank and some cotton pants.", "reference": "2022, Robyn Henderson-Espinoza, Body Becoming: A Path to Our Liberation, Minneapolis, Minn.: Broadleaf Books, 1517 Media, →ISBN:"}, {"text": "On TikTok, #wifepleaser boasts more than 11.4 million views, while #wifepleasertank has racked up 13.9 million. […] Thanks to TikTok, there has been a mass adoption of the term “wife pleaser” in an attempt to rebrand the tank.", "reference": "2023 August 9, Brooke Kato, “Gen Z loves the ‘wife beater’ tee — but they’re canceling the name”, in New York Post, New York, N.Y.: News Corp, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 10 Aug 2023:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["battle tank", "combat tank", "armour", "tango"], "antonyms": ["glass cannon"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈtæŋk/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈtʰæŋk]", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈteɪ̯ŋk/", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈtʰeɪ̯ŋk]", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈtɛ̃ŋk/", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈtʰɛ̃ŋk]", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "tanks", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "tanking", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "tanked", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "tanked", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To fail or fall (often used in describing the economy or the stock market); to degenerate or decline rapidly; to plummet.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "He told me about all the odd jobs he'd taken after I was born, when Michigan's economy was tanking. For one, he crisscrossed the Midwest buying old carpets from dentists' offices.", "reference": "2008 October, Davy Rothbart, “How I caught up with dad”, in Men's Health, volume 23, number 8, →ISSN, page 112:"}, {"text": "\"[...] If the economy has tanked... then we don't want to over-promise and under-deliver.\"", "reference": "2022 October 5, “Network News: Private sector's role in a publicly-owned railway”, in RAIL, number 967, page 16:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "спадам"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "dégringoler"}, {"language": {"code": "ta", "name": "Tamil"}, "word": "தோல்"}, {"language": {"code": "ta", "name": "Tamil"}, "word": "வீழ்"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(video games) To attract the attacks of an enemy target in cooperative team-based combat, so that one's teammates can defeat the enemy in question more efficiently.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "pansre"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "modstå"}, {"language": {"code": "it", "name": "Italian"}, "word": "tankare"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "tankar"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "tanquear"}, {"language": {"code": "tr", "name": "Turkish"}, "word": "tanklamak"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive) To put (fuel, etc.) into a tank.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": ["Concrete below ground must be fully tanked to prevent water uptake."], "quotes": [{"text": "Sometimes oils are tanked for months or years at a time (e.g., linseed oil).", "reference": "1913, Geoffrey Martin, Industrial and manufacturing chemistry:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To deliberately lose a sports match with the intent of gaining a perceived future competitive advantage.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Beforehand, Swedish [national ice hockey team] coach Bengt-Ake Gustafsson had ruminated about tanking against Slovakia to avoid powerful Canada or the Czechs in the quarters [i.e., quarterfinals of the 2006 Winter Olympic tournament], telling Swedish television, \"One is cholera, the other the plague.\"", "reference": "2006 March 6, Michael Farber, “Swede Success”, in (Please provide the book title or journal name), Sports Illustrated, archived from the original on 04 Nov 2012:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(fandom slang) To resist damage; to be attacked without being hurt.", "tags": ["slang"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Unless Bane can tank Helicarrier-busting explosions I'm not sure how he stands a chance.", "reference": "2015 March 1, DudeFuckMath, “Bane [DC] vs Iron Fist [Marvel]”, in Reddit (r/whowouldwin), retrieved 19 Jun 2017:"}, {"text": "A weakened Superman tanked an explosion 50 times larger than the Kepler's Supernova and the electromagnetic shock wave hit him.", "reference": "2016 June 2, MercinWithAMouth, “Superman Stongest Feat Ever”, in Comic Vine Forums, retrieved 19 Jun 2017:"}, {"text": "Barda could BFR and I doubt She hulk is tanking a blow from her rod, so she takes.", "reference": "2016 July 22, Si-Phon Dom, “Big Barda Vs She Hulk”, in Comics Amino, retrieved 19 Jun 2017:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "arrostrar"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(originally poker, slang) To contemplate a decision for a long time; to go in the tank.", "tags": ["slang"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(Singapore, colloquial) To stand; to tolerate.", "tags": ["Singapore", "colloquial"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(Singapore, colloquial) To willingly take on an undesirable task or burden.", "tags": ["Singapore", "colloquial"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈtæŋk/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈtʰæŋk]", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈteɪ̯ŋk/", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈtʰeɪ̯ŋk]", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈtɛ̃ŋk/", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈtʰɛ̃ŋk]", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "tanks", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "A small Indian dry measure, averaging 240 grains in weight.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A Bombay weight of 72 grains, for pearls.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}